---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="About Us & Our Methodology"
  description="Science-backed guidance on the best indoor plants for cleaner air, better sleep, and a healthier home. Learn about our mission, methodology, and editorial standards."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 pb-20">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-green-600 mb-3">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-stone-900 mb-4">Our Mission</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">We believe every home deserves cleaner air -- and the simplest solution has been growing in gardens for thousands of years.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose prose-stone max-w-none">
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Air Purifying Plants Guide is built on a simple premise: the NASA Clean Air Study proved that common houseplants filter dangerous chemicals from indoor air, yet most people do not know which plants to choose or how to care for them.
      </p>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We bridge that gap. Every plant on this site is backed by the original 1989 NASA research and subsequent peer-reviewed studies. Our care guides are practical, our toxicity warnings are clear, and our recommendations are honest.
      </p>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Indoor air is typically 2-5 times more polluted than outdoor air, according to the EPA. The good news: the solution is beautiful, affordable, and proven by science.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">How We Select and Score Plants</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We only include plants that appeared in the NASA Clean Air Study or subsequent peer-reviewed research on indoor air phytoremediation. Each plant's <strong>Air Purification Score (1-10)</strong> is based on three weighted factors:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-stone-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
        <li><strong>Number of VOCs filtered (40%)</strong> -- plants that remove multiple pollutants score higher</li>
        <li><strong>Filtration efficiency in studies (35%)</strong> -- measured removal rates for top pollutants</li>
        <li><strong>Additional benefits (25%)</strong> -- nighttime oxygen production, humidity regulation, mold spore reduction</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        <strong>Care difficulty</strong> is rated Easy (1), Moderate (2), or Needs Care (3) based on watering frequency, light sensitivity, humidity requirements, and tolerance for common mistakes.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Editorial Standards</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        All content on this site is researched and fact-checked against primary sources. We cite the original NASA Clean Air Study (Wolverton, Johnson, and Bounds, 1989) and subsequent research published in peer-reviewed journals including <em>Environmental Science and Pollution Research</em> and the <em>Journal of the American Society for Horticultural Science</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Toxicity information is cross-referenced with the ASPCA's Animal Poison Control Center database for pets and scientific literature for human toxicity concerns. Care recommendations are reviewed against guidance from the Royal Horticultural Society and university extension programs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Our Commitment to Accuracy</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We are transparent about the limitations of the NASA study: real homes are not sealed chambers, and ventilation reduces per-plant effectiveness. We never claim a single plant will "cure" indoor air pollution. Instead, we provide the realistic, evidence-based guidance you need to make informed decisions about improving your home's air quality with plants.
      </p>
      <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        This site is independently maintained and updated regularly. If you spot an error or have a question about our methodology, we welcome your feedback.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>